  "reason": "The existing evidence shows that an RNA-only model with PCA encoding achieves moderate performance (0.4849 accuracy). The next experiment should test whether adding image data (via multimodal fusion) improves performance, as this directly addresses the uncertainty about multimodal efficacy. Config_016 introduces a simple multimodal setup with the same RNA encoder (pca_n2000) and image encoder (resnet50), using concatenation fusion. This isolates the effect of multimodal components while keeping other design choices minimal, allowing a direct comparison against the RNA-only baseline."
